## chart main MMDX Concept Map
```mermaid
flowchart TD
  crowded["Plain Mermaid gets crowded"]
  wrapper["MMDX: ordinary Mermaid charts plus metadata links"]
  source["Source contract"]
  encode["Encoding contract"]
  viewer["Viewer runtime"]
  bridge["Local bridge"]
  failure["Failure map"]
  threshold["Use threshold"]
  cadence["Authoring cadence"]
  fork["Not a Mermaid fork"]
  outcome["Clickable drilldown without cloning syntax"]

  crowded --> wrapper
  wrapper --> source
  wrapper --> encode
  wrapper --> viewer
  viewer --> bridge
  wrapper --> failure
  wrapper --> threshold
  wrapper --> cadence
  wrapper --> fork
  source --> outcome
  encode --> outcome
  viewer --> outcome
  bridge --> outcome
  threshold --> outcome
  cadence --> outcome
  failure -. protects .-> outcome
  fork -. keeps charts portable .-> outcome

  classDef problem fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px
  classDef contract fill:#e0f2fe,stroke:#0284c7,color:#0c4a6e,stroke-width:2px
  classDef runtime fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d,stroke-width:2px
  classDef analysis fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef principle fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#3b0764,stroke-width:2px
  classDef result fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:3px

  class crowded problem
  class source,encode contract
  class viewer,bridge runtime
  class failure,threshold,cadence analysis
  class wrapper,fork principle
  class outcome result
```

## chart source-contract MMDX Source Contract
```mermaid
erDiagram
  MMDX_DOCUMENT ||--|| METADATA : "declares entry"
  MMDX_DOCUMENT ||--|{ CHART : "contains"
  METADATA ||--o{ LINK : "declares"
  LINK }o--|| CHART : "from chart"
  LINK }o--|| CHART : "to chart"

  MMDX_DOCUMENT {
    string path
    string markdown
  }

  METADATA {
    string entry
    array links
  }

  CHART {
    string id PK
    string title
    string mermaid_code
  }

  LINK {
    string from FK
    string label
    string to FK
    string title
  }
```

## chart chart-contract Chart Object Contract
```mermaid
classDiagram
  class MMDXDocument {
    +int version
    +string entry
    +MermaidChart[] charts
    +MmdxLink[] links
  }

  class MermaidChart {
    +string id
    +string title
    +string code
  }

  class MmdxLink {
    +string from
    +string label
    +string to
    +string title
  }

  class MermaidParser {
    +preflight(code)
    +detectDiagramType(code)
  }

  MMDXDocument "1" *-- "*" MermaidChart : carries
  MMDXDocument "1" *-- "*" MmdxLink : wires
  MermaidParser ..> MermaidChart : validates code
  MmdxLink ..> MermaidChart : from and to ids
```

## chart encoding-contract Encoding Contract Over Time
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Author
  participant Script as mmd.py
  participant Parser as Mermaid parser
  participant State as URL state
  participant Viewer as buildooor /diagrams

  Author->>Script: pass .mmdx source
  Script->>Script: parse metadata and chart fences
  Script->>Parser: preflight every chart
  Parser-->>Script: diagram types OK
  Script->>State: code = entry chart
  Script->>State: buildooorMmdx = stack
  Script->>State: pako: fragment
  State-->>Viewer: open /diagrams#pako...
  Viewer->>Viewer: decode entry and private stack
```

## chart byte-pipeline Byte Pipeline
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  state["State object"]
  code["code: entry chart"]
  mmdx["buildooorMmdx"]
  config["mermaid config"]
  handoff["optional handoff and source metadata"]
  json["JSON stringify with compact separators"]
  utf8["UTF-8 bytes"]
  deflate["zlib DEFLATE level 9"]
  b64["URL-safe base64 without padding"]
  pako["pako: fragment"]

  state --> code
  state --> mmdx
  state --> config
  state --> handoff
  state --> json --> utf8 --> deflate --> b64 --> pako

  classDef payload fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#3b0764,stroke-width:2px
  classDef transform fill:#e0f2fe,stroke:#0284c7,color:#0c4a6e,stroke-width:2px
  classDef output fill:#d1fae5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:3px
  class state,code,mmdx,config,handoff payload
  class json,utf8,deflate,b64 transform
  class pako output
```

## chart payload-fields URL State Field Responsibilities
```mermaid
classDiagram
  class MermaidLiveState {
    +string code
    +string mermaid
    +bool grid
    +bool panZoom
    +bool rough
    +bool updateDiagram
    +BuildooorMmdx buildooorMmdx
    +BuildooorHandoff buildooorHandoff
    +BuildooorSource buildooorSource
  }

  class BuildooorMmdx {
    +int version
    +string entry
    +Chart[] charts
    +Link[] links
  }

  class BuildooorSource {
    +string path
    +string cwd
  }

  class BuildooorHandoff {
    +string endpoint
    +string token
    +string tmuxTarget
    +string[] capabilities
  }

  MermaidLiveState *-- BuildooorMmdx : carries stack
  MermaidLiveState o-- BuildooorSource : optional file identity
  MermaidLiveState o-- BuildooorHandoff : optional edit channel
```

## chart viewer-runtime Browser Runtime State Machine
```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Entry chart" as EntryChart
  state "Linked label" as LinkedLabel
  state "Child chart" as ChildChart
  state "Back" as Back
  state "Source edit mode" as SourceEdit
  state "Wand drilldown packet" as WandPacket

  [*] --> EntryChart
  EntryChart --> LinkedLabel: click marked text
  LinkedLabel --> ChildChart: resolve metadata target
  ChildChart --> Back: inspect detail
  Back --> EntryChart: return
  EntryChart --> SourceEdit: bridge metadata present
  SourceEdit --> WandPacket: ask for one useful child
  WandPacket --> EntryChart: reopen patched stack
```

## chart link-resolution Link Resolution Detail
```mermaid
flowchart TD
  link["MmdxLink: from + label + to"]
  source["Active chart id equals from"]
  render["Viewer renders Mermaid SVG"]
  scan["Find visible SVG text exactly matching label"]
  clickable["Attach click handler and title"]
  target["Load target chart id"]
  mismatch["MISMATCH: no clickable target"]

  link --> source --> render --> scan
  scan --> clickable --> target
  scan -. no exact text .-> mismatch

  classDef contract fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#3b0764,stroke-width:2px
  classDef runtime fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d,stroke-width:2px
  classDef error fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px

  class link,source contract
  class render,scan,clickable,target runtime
  class mismatch error
```

## chart local-bridge Local Bridge Handoff
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User
  participant Viewer as buildooor /diagrams
  participant Bridge as localhost bridge
  participant File as attached .mmdx file
  participant Tmux as tmux pane

  User->>Viewer: select notes, send, or wand
  Viewer->>Bridge: token and origin check
  Viewer->>Bridge: POST /source/read
  Bridge->>File: read attached path only
  File-->>Bridge: full MMDX document
  Bridge-->>Viewer: source text
  Viewer->>Bridge: POST /source/write
  Bridge->>Bridge: preflight submitted stack
  Bridge->>File: write only if valid
  Viewer->>Bridge: send edit packet
  Bridge->>Tmux: paste into target pane
```

## chart source-write-gates Source Write Gates
```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Submitted code" as SubmittedCode
  state "Origin and token OK" as TokenOk
  state "Preflight every chart" as PreflightEveryChart
  state "Preflight failed" as PreflightFailed
  state "Write attached source" as WriteAttachedSource
  state "Reopen stack" as ReopenStack

  [*] --> SubmittedCode
  SubmittedCode --> TokenOk
  TokenOk --> PreflightEveryChart
  PreflightEveryChart --> PreflightFailed: parser error
  PreflightEveryChart --> WriteAttachedSource: OK
  WriteAttachedSource --> ReopenStack
  PreflightFailed --> SubmittedCode: patch source
```

## chart failure-map MMDX Drilldown Failure Map
```mermaid
ishikawa-beta
  MMDX drilldown fails
    Source
      HIGH: malformed metadata JSON
      HIGH: chart id missing
      MED: entry points to wrong chart
    Link matching
      HIGH: label mismatch
      MED: duplicate visible labels
      MED: link points to the right chart but wrong concept
    Validation
      HIGH: no preflight
      MED: unsupported Mermaid syntax
      UNKNOWN: renderer behavior differs from parser
    Browser
      MED: selected SVG text is split
      LOW: pan zoom hides context
    Bridge
      MED: handoff expired
      HIGH: source path not attached
    Design
      MED: child repeats parent
      HIGH: every label becomes a link
```

## chart use-threshold MMDX Use Threshold
```mermaid
quadrantChart
  title When MMDX Beats One Mermaid Chart
  x-axis Simple story --> Many lenses
  y-axis Low consequence --> Decision leverage
  quadrant-1 MMDX zone
  quadrant-2 Maybe split
  quadrant-3 One chart
  quadrant-4 Appendix
  "Use one .mmd": [0.18, 0.22]
  "Maybe split later": [0.37, 0.64]
  "MMDX pays off": [0.82, 0.88]
  "Docs appendix only": [0.72, 0.32]
```

## chart authoring-cadence MMDX Authoring Cadence
```mermaid
gantt
  title MMDX Authoring Cadence
  dateFormat  YYYY-MM-DD
  axisFormat  %b %d

  section Shape
  Choose entry decision surface :done, choose, 2026-05-02, 1d
  Pick child chart families     :active, families, after choose, 1d

  section Source
  Write named chart fences      :write, after families, 1d
  Add exact visible links       :links, after write, 1d

  section Proof
  Validate every chart          :crit, validate, after links, 1d
  Open and inspect              :inspect, after validate, 1d
  Patch one child               :milestone, patch, after inspect, 0d
```

## chart stack-design Stack Design Principles
```mermaid
mindmap
  root((Stack design))
    Entry chart
      Decision surface
      Not an index
    Link policy
      Few labels
      Exact visible text
      High leverage only
    Child charts
      Child chart changes type
      Answer why
      Answer what next
      Answer what blocks it
    Depth
      Start with one or two levels
      Add a child when the question changes
```

